NOTE ON THE DISTRIBUTED COMBINATION

This project's own source files are MIT, as above.

The **distributed combination is AGPL-3.0**, because the analysis worker
includes Essentia (AGPL-3.0, https://github.com/MTG/essentia). Essentia is
invoked as an unmodified standalone binary over a subprocess boundary
(argv in, JSON out) and is never linked into this codebase.

Practically this means: if you deploy this and other people use it over a
network, you must offer them the Corresponding Source. A "Source" link in the
footer pointing at this repository, pinned to the deployed commit, satisfies
that.

Keeping this project's own files MIT means that if Essentia is ever swapped
out, relicensing is a one-line change here rather than obtaining consent from
every contributor.

Other components and their licences are listed in docs/PRD.md section 7.3.
